 "description": "Two obj tiers share one bucket under different prefixes, one with no prefix. A promotion refused at submission (transfer() fails) is reported at the next poll before a cascade WRITE that was submitted earlier and finished: the tier queues submission failures as they happen and appends polled completions after them. The refused promotion's verdict becomes a miss. Then both tiers' transfers are held in flight across steps (a slow WRITE) and reset_cache drains them: drain_jobs blocks until the WRITEs finish, and their results reach the manager at the next poll; until the reset is flushed, every lookup misses (promotions are held, manager.py:590-640@4ba787ec).",
